window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["seat-cupra/exeo-3r"]={"exeo-3r-activate-comfort-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Function:</strong> Activates the convenience turn signals.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select <strong>Channel 12</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>","exeo-3r-activate-turn-signals-in-us-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates US indicators  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Replace the last coding digit (xxxxx?) with<strong> 3</strong></p>","exeo-3r-automatic-door-locks":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+32</strong> to the existing coding </em>:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/codage-vcds_Audi-A4-B6-Confirmation-de-verrouillag-aea7b330.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-automatic-headlamp-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p>Purpose: to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p>5 – Select <strong>Channel 20</strong> “Rain/Light Sensor Setup” from the drop-down list</p>\n<p><em>Add<strong> +1</strong> to existing value</em></p>","exeo-3r-aux-in-socket-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to activate the AUX-IN input. After installing the jack plug on the car radio connector or a Bluetooth kit (RNS-E or Generation II+ Concert, Chorus and Symphony), you can select AUX-IN in Source. For a BT module, if you have the AMI option, deactivate it.   (Retrofit)</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (For RNS-E !) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Modify the penultimate digit by adding <strong>4</strong>(e.g. replace <strong>xxxxx1x</strong>with <strong>xxxxx5x</strong>). </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_tt_8j_stg37_navi_codierung_auxin-f8795b14.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (For Generation II+ Concert, Chorus and Symphony</strong>)<strong>:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on<strong>“56 – Radio</strong>” .<br/><br/> 4<strong>– </strong>Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>“.  </p>\n<p>5 – Modify the second digit by adding <strong>+4</strong> (0<strong>?</strong>x0xxx): <strong><br/><br/>+1 = Analog input (AUX)</strong><br/>+2 = Multifunction steering wheel<br/>+4 = Telephone</p>","exeo-3r-change-rns-e-startup-screen":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to change the screen display at RNS-E start-up.  </p>\n<p><strong><em><em>CAUTION (Some RNS-E settings are directly related to the selected model. It is not recommended to change the vehicle model (Line 1)). </em> </em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Change the 2nd digit to the desired model. (ex: replace<strong>02xxxxx</strong>by<strong>01xxxxx</strong>to display the Lamborghini logo on an A3) </p>\n<p>– 1 Lamborghini Galardo<br/>– 2 <em>Audi A3 (8P)</em><br/>– 3 Audi A4 (8E) or Seat Exeo (3R)<br/>– 4 Audi A4 Cabriolet (8H)<br/>– 5 Audi A6 (4B)<br/>– 6 Audi TT (8J)<br/>– 7 Audi R8 (42)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” .<br/><br/> 4<strong>– </strong>Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 18</strong> (Start Screen) then set the value according to the desired display. <br/><br/>– 0 Standard<br/>– 1 Audi S3 (8P)<br/>– 2 Audi S4 (8E)<br/>– 3 Audi RS4, (8E)<br/>– 4 Audi TT (8J)<br/>– 5 Audi R8 (42)<br/>– 7 Audi TT S (8J)<br/>– 8 Audi TT RS (8J)<br/>– 9 Audi R8 GT (<em>42</em>)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8P0-035-193-G_Module37_Adaptation_Channel18-4f78df82.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-comfort-closure-confirmation":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates comfort closing confirmation. The indicators will light up (x1) when the windows and sunroof are fully closed.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+512</strong> to the existing coding </em>:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/codage-vcds_Audi-A4-B6-Confirmation-de-verrouillag-aea7b330.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-coming-home-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is locked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01</strong> (Coming-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","exeo-3r-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em><em>Put <strong>4 in </strong>the last digit of the code (00xxxx<strong>?</strong>).</em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instrument-Coding_A4_B7-4e018a9f.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglaceaudia4-72b9f760.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em><em>Put <strong>0 in </strong>the penultimate digit of the code (00xxx<strong>?</strong>x).</em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instrument-Coding_A4_B7-4e018a9f.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-display-night-light-indicator-on-speedometer":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to display the pilot light on the counter.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Remove <strong>02 </strong>from digits in position 3-4 of the code (00<strong>??</strong>xxx).</em></p>\n<p><em>(Ex: <strong>0023004</strong>becomes <strong>0021004</strong>)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instrument-Coding_A4_B7-4e018a9f.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables vehicle lock/unlock confirmation with beeps.  </p>\n<p><strong>The vehicle must be equipped with the factory-installed alarm</strong>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+1024</strong> to the existing coding </em>:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/codage-vcds_Audi-A4-B6-Confirmation-de-verrouillag-aea7b330.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>activates confirmation of vehicle locking/unlocking with turn signals.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+2</strong> to the existing coding </em>:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/codage-vcds_Audi-A4-B6-Confirmation-de-verrouillag-aea7b330.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-lights-come-on-automatically-when-it-rains":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically turns on the headlights when it rains.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p>5 – Select <strong>Channel 20</strong> “Rain/Light Sensor Setup” from the drop-down list</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>+2</strong> to the existing value</em></p>","exeo-3r-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-rns-e":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To lock/unlock the RNS-E’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 67</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>255</strong> <em>(Eject Button locked i.e. (Rental Car))</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS-E.</em></p>\n<p>To eject the CD/DVD, set the value to <strong>0</strong> for normal use of the button, or <strong>1</strong> to eject it immediately.  </p>","exeo-3r-memory-1-on-odb-of-km-traveled":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates memory 1 for km covered, average speed, time since start… These memories will be reset after an engine shutdown lasting more than 2 hours.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choose <strong>Channel 19</strong></p>\n<p><em>In the second digit of the code (x<strong>?</strong>xxx), enter the value according to the desired option:<br/> 0 = Memory 2 only (permanent memory)<br/> 1 = Memory 1 + Memory 2</em></p>","exeo-3r-meter-lighting":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to change the illumination of the hands and dial.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>17 – Instruments.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10 </strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select <strong>Channel 19 </strong>:</p>\n<p><em>Set the first digit of the code (<strong>?</strong>xxxx) to the value corresponding to the desired display:<br/><strong>0</strong> = Hands off and dial off (with the ignition on and headlights off)<br/><strong>1</strong> = Hands on and dial off (with the ignition on and headlights off)<br/><strong>2</strong> = Hands off and dial on (ignition on, headlights off)<br/><strong>3</strong> = Dials and needles on (ignition on, headlights off)</em></p>","exeo-3r-selective-door-locking-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>activates selective locking/unlocking of doors.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+4</strong> to the existing coding </em>:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/codage-vcds_Audi-A4-B6-Confirmation-de-verrouillag-aea7b330.webp\"/></figure>","exeo-3r-speed-limit-display-rns-e":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS-E navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>ATTENTION: requires RNS-E version 193</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4<strong>– </strong>Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 17</strong> (Speed Display) then set the value according to the desired display. <br/><br/>Set the value according to the desired display<em><br/>0</em><em>– no option (display disabled)<br/></em> 1<em>– option on, off (speed display)<br/></em> 2<em>– option on, off, 5km/h, 10km/h, 15km/h, 20km/h (speed display + overrun warning)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8P0-035-193-G_Module37_Adaptation_Channel17-6e590288.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Don’t forget to restart the RNS-E, by pressing the power button for more than 40s.</em></p>","exeo-3r-tear-wiping":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the windshield wipers once more after using the windshield washer, in order to remove any remaining water from the windshield.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p>5 – Select <strong>Channel 13</strong> “Wiper Setup” from the drop-down list</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>+8</strong> to existing value</em></p>"};
